From: relay12 contributors
Subject: [PATCH] d3d11on12: route the GetProcAddress cast through void*

GCC rejects casting FARPROC straight to PCOMPATVALUE under
-Wcast-function-type: FARPROC is INT_PTR(WINAPI*)() and the target has a
different signature. Casting via void* is the accepted spelling and is
already what patches/dtl/0007 does for its own GetProcAddress wrapper, so the
two ports stay consistent.

Behaviour is unchanged. dxgi.dll's CompatValue is resolved by name at run
time either way, and the function is still treated as absent when the export
is missing.
---
diff --git a/src/main.cpp b/src/main.cpp
index c4f397a..34f150a 100644
--- a/src/main.cpp
+++ b/src/main.cpp
@@ -20,7 +20,12 @@ bool GetCompatValue(const char* str, UINT64* pValue)
     static PCOMPATVALUE pfnCompatValue = nullptr;
     if (!pfnCompatValue)
     {
-        pfnCompatValue = reinterpret_cast<PCOMPATVALUE>(GetProcAddress(GetModuleHandleW(L"dxgi.dll"), "CompatValue"));
+        // GCC rejects a direct FARPROC-to-PCOMPATVALUE cast under
+        // -Wcast-function-type. Going through void* is the same idiom
+        // the D3D12TranslationLayer port uses for GetProcAddress.
+        pfnCompatValue = reinterpret_cast<PCOMPATVALUE>(
+                reinterpret_cast<void *>(GetProcAddress(
+                        GetModuleHandleW(L"dxgi.dll"), "CompatValue")));
     }
     if (pfnCompatValue)
     {
